  "overchargedIdCollision": {
    "description": "The same shape as `scannerIdCollision` and by far the commoner case: the game writes `Weapon_Overcharged` for every weapon's Overcharged, but a multi-cannon's also cuts the clip 3-15% and a cannon's does not, so `blueprints.jsonc` keys the clip-carrying side under `MC_Overcharged` — the spelling the multi-cannon menus list. 70 of the build corpus's 1902 declared entries need this resolution, against one for the scanners. Each case pins the id as a journal writes it, the `BLUEPRINTS` key the fitted module actually rolls, and the exact `Engineering.Modifiers` block that follows at the pinned grade and quality. The anti-xeno multi-cannon is the case that rests on one registry: coriolis-data carries no blueprint list for an anti-xeno group, EDSY's single Overcharged carries the clip leg wherever it is offered, and following the sole covering registry is what puts this module on the clip-carrying record. The cannon, the fragment cannon and the plasma accelerator are the controls: same id, same three legs, and no `AmmoClipSize`, on the three clip-carrying groups that take this recipe. Frontier's own reading backs each — `journal-federation-corvette.jsonc` carries a large gimballed cannon rolled to grade 5 under this id with no `AmmoClipSize` modifier and its stock magazine of 5 still loaded, where a 15% cut would have left four rounds; `journal-federation-corvette-plasma.jsonc` carries a medium fragment cannon rolled to grade 4 whose modifier block likewise has none; and `journal-caspian-explorer.jsonc` carries a medium fixed plasma accelerator rolled to grade 1 at quality 1, whose three recipe legs this library reproduces to the digit and which carries none either. On those two the magazine is too small for the loaded count to corroborate the absent leg — a −12% cut leaves 3 × 0.88 = 2.64 and a −3% cut leaves 5 × 0.97 = 4.85, and both round back — so there it is the modifier list that carries the case. EDSY holds that a cannon's clip should drop here; coriolis-data and EDEngineer, which key a recipe per weapon type rather than per recipe id, stop the leg at the multi-cannon, and all three captures agree with them.",
